{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 67, :comments ["<b>And he brought her, the tent of Sarah his mother.</b> Every word that requires a mem at the beginning, he prefixed a vav, etc. The meaning: he brought her into the designated tent, which was Sarah his mother's." "<b>Sarah his mother.</b> As long as she was alive, a lamp would burn from Sabbath eve to Sabbath eve, and a blessing was found in the dough, and a cloud was bound over the tent — corresponding to the observance of the commandments: the dough is challah, the lamp is lighting the Sabbath lamp. The bound cloud is a model of the menstrual laws, for their sign comes and goes, ceases and returns." "<b>And Yitzhak was comforted after his mother.</b> After she resembled her mother in her deeds."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {1 "The comment identifies three signs linked to three commandments; the phrase 'הדלקת הנר' is written after 'חלה' with no conjunction, suggesting it refers back to the lamp mentioned earlier. The word עיסה in the first clause and חלה in the second both refer to dough, connected to the commandment of challah."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:46.843813053Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}